{"id": "EUVD-2026-102266", "enisaUuid": "50b56752-afc3-39d4-8d70-8906a9aed2ee", "description": "NetSurf libnsbmp through 0.1.7 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in bmp_decode_mask() that allows attackers to read one byte past the image buffer by supplying crafted ICO files. Attackers can provide an ICO whose inner bitmap width is not a multiple of 8, causing a heap over-read that can crash applications calling bmp_decode().", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:57:31", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libnsbmp-rle-absolute-pad-and-ico-mask-oob-read", "https://github.com/netsurf-browser/libnsbmp/blob/ea063c9f46acb43e90208da14073332b505ef7e7/src/libnsbmp.c#L835-L873", "https://download.netsurf-browser.org/libs/releases/libnsbmp-0.1.7-src.tar.gz", "https://github.com/netsurf-browser/libnsbmp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netsurf-libnsbmp-through-0.1.7-out-of-bounds-read-via-bmp-decode-mask"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j4g8-9gm4-w4v9", "CVE-2026-111139"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c925114d-4f63-3c24-aa0e-fdb4edc4c008", "product": {"name": "Libnsbmp", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d272314-3604-36b8-b43b-29c25746888f", "vendor": {"name": "netsurf"}}], "isExploited": false}